# Pairs with CursorNeverSkipsUnshipped. Reproduces production before #4477 (#4465). A
# duplicate of an entry whose first delivery is still between its dependency
# check and its buffer insert finds the identity reservation that delivery
# took, is classified as a duplicate and acknowledged, and the ack moves the
# shipper's cursor past the entry. A restart of the receiver then aborts the
# first delivery, which was never acknowledged, so nothing re-sends it.
MODULE: CursorNeverSkipsUnshippedDuplicateOfParkingAcked
TARGET: CursorNeverSkipsUnshipped
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: acknowledges a duplicate of an entry still being parked, so a restart loses the entry the cursor has passed
PERTURBS: Deliver

--- FIND
          \/ w.o = x
       /\ ~InFlight(x, w)
--- REPLACE
          \/ w.o = x
\* MUTATION: an in-flight duplicate is processed (and acknowledged) at once.
--- END
